WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:05.359
Hey youtubers it's Charlie and avatar wisdom
is a thing of the past.

00:00:05.359 --> 00:00:06.839
I mean book 3 is here.

00:00:06.839 --> 00:00:10.100
They aired the first three episodes back to
back.

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:13.420
This video will be my review of the first
two and instead of a Q&amp;A tomorrow I'm going

00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:16.550
to post a review of Episode 3.

00:00:16.550 --> 00:00:20.370
Hello to all the new people, if you're just
now finding me, I do Legend of Korra videos

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:21.370
every week.

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:22.593
I'm also doing a weekly giveaway for each
episode.

00:00:22.593 --> 00:00:26.550
All you have to do to participate is be a
subscriber and leave a comment on this video.

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:29.670
I'll explain again at the end of this video.

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:33.320
We've got a lot of stuff to talk about so
this is what I'm going to do.

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:37.969
I'll start with top 10 moments from episodes
1 and 2, then I'll do a review and then I'll

00:00:37.969 --> 00:00:39.350
talk about the biggest stuff coming in Book
3.

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:41.379
So careful for spoilers from the episode if
you haven't seen it yet.

00:00:41.379 --> 00:00:42.390
But here we go.

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:44.329
Number 10 - Korasami Driving Lessons

00:00:44.329 --> 00:00:48.789
I know all the Korasami 'shippers from Books
1 and 2 flipped a little when they realized

00:00:48.789 --> 00:00:51.319
how close Korra and Asami were going to be
in Book 3.

00:00:51.319 --> 00:00:54.579
The driving lessons spells out their dynamic
perfectly.

00:00:54.579 --> 00:01:00.579
They both like to poke fun at each other but
neither is upset about the other one hooking

00:01:00.579 --> 00:01:07.000
up with Mako while they were both dating him.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:10.799
I feel like if you did a Korra power rankings
list, Mako would have just shot straight to

00:01:10.799 --> 00:01:14.060
the bottom in the first few moments of the
episode.

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:17.810
It's not super clear what his character arc
is going to be this year, but I feel kind

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:18.810
of bad for him.

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:21.690
I will enjoy Korra and Asami torturing him
a little.

00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:27.710
What are friends for if not for embarrasing
you every chance they get.

00:01:27.710 --> 00:01:33.329
Korra also called it out, she's never had
a real girl who was a friend she could talk

00:01:33.329 --> 00:01:34.329
to.

00:01:34.329 --> 00:01:35.329
That's depressing.

00:01:35.329 --> 00:01:40.450
But based on the first couple of episodes,
it seems like Asami will be spending the most

00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:42.170
amount of time with Korra on screen.

00:01:42.170 --> 00:01:44.700
Like most of Korra's scenes will also involve
Asami.

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:55.031
I'm really glad they didn't just talk about
relationships, I feel like on a lot of younger

00:01:55.031 --> 00:02:01.070
shows the female characters spend too much
time talking about male characters and not

00:02:01.070 --> 00:02:02.940
enough about their own interests.

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:06.439
I think one of the best things about Legend
of Korra is that it portrays a very positive

00:02:06.439 --> 00:02:08.220
female perspective.

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:14.890
For instance, Asami had the idea to use Korra's
Dark Spirit calming technique to get the vines

00:02:14.890 --> 00:02:15.890
to go away.

00:02:15.890 --> 00:02:19.670
And it didn't require a suggestion from a
male character.

00:02:19.670 --> 00:02:22.190
Number 9 - Tenzin Talking To Aang's Statue

00:02:22.190 --> 00:02:27.220
This was just heartwarming, Tenzin speaking
to the spirit of Aang while looking at his

00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:28.500
Statue in the bay.

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:32.180
It's unclear exactly what happened to Korra's
past lives and the spirits of the former avatars,

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:34.890
but you're not really thinking about that
in this moment.

00:02:34.890 --> 00:02:38.940
Whenever he started talking I instantly thought
about the moment where Aang realized that

00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:40.940
the entire Air Nation had been killed.

00:02:40.940 --> 00:02:43.460
It was so heartbreaking and now, thanks to
Korra's actions.

00:02:43.460 --> 00:02:44.460
They're coming back.

00:02:44.460 --> 00:02:49.900
It's still really unclear why Harmonic Convergence
caused people to manifest airbending and no

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:51.640
other bending forms.

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:55.190
I think that will be something it takes all
season to find out.

00:02:55.190 --> 00:03:00.330
For now though, we get to enjoy the resolution
of a plot point that served as the basis for

00:03:00.330 --> 00:03:02.780
Avatar The Last Airbender.

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:05.341
Number 8 - Look at this effing Airbending
Hipster

00:03:05.341 --> 00:03:10.220
This was one of those scenes that makes you
want to shoot this kid and laugh out loud

00:03:10.220 --> 00:03:11.220
at the same moment.

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:12.670
Not at the same time, we're not psycho's here.

00:03:12.670 --> 00:03:16.100
I feel like this is Mike and Bryan and the
writers making fun of twenty somethings in

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:17.240
general.

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:22.100
Or maybe they were making fun of themselves
for living in their parent's houses way longer

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:23.100
than they should have.

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:25.941
I don't know a lot about Mike and Bryan or
the writers before Last Airbender or Korra

00:03:25.941 --> 00:03:26.941
started.

00:03:26.941 --> 00:03:31.400
The whole idea of people not wanting to become
part of the Air Nation was kind of infuriating

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:34.170
and this hipster kid was just the worst of
it.

00:03:34.170 --> 00:03:40.480
He was nuttier than the farmer who started
shouting because he was so angry.

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:43.790
Number 7 - Tenzin Is the World's Worst Salesman

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:47.640
This was one of the most gif'able montages
in all of the new episodes.

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:51.590
You get to be a vegetarian, you get tattoos
all over your body, you get to give away all

00:03:51.590 --> 00:03:54.040
your possessions, you get these amazing robes.

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:59.070
The only one of his pitches that I thought
was good was the Giant Air Bison being your

00:03:59.070 --> 00:04:00.070
best friend.

00:04:00.070 --> 00:04:03.040
I would totally want an air bison as a best
friend.

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:04.930
You could name it appa jr.

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:09.250
All of the refusals reminded me of Yoda's
quote from Empire Strikes Back, "Too Old To

00:04:09.250 --> 00:04:10.300
Begin the Training."

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:16.040
It's a metaphor that once you become an adult
you become to closeminded about the idea of

00:04:16.040 --> 00:04:17.380
a new reality.

00:04:17.380 --> 00:04:20.959
Which was exactly what Zaheer said to the
White Lotus guards when he escaped.

00:04:20.959 --> 00:04:23.920
It just makes me feel like a big part of Book
3 will be Korra teaching people to open up

00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:25.810
to new possibilities.

00:04:25.810 --> 00:04:31.130
Number 6 - The Avatar Circus Performers

00:04:31.130 --> 00:04:34.200
This really reminded me of the play from Last
Airbender.

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:39.590
In that episode the play was based very literally
on the adventures of Team Avatar, and on Korra

00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:43.150
the play was a closer approximation of her
battle with Amon.

00:04:43.150 --> 00:04:48.070
Watching this made me realize we need more
mustache Bolin, shirtless Tenzin was a little

00:04:48.070 --> 00:04:53.530
weird given I keep think of JK Simmons when
he talks.

00:04:53.530 --> 00:05:01.390
I love how Bolin is still reveling in theatricality
like when he was doing Nuktuk.

00:05:01.390 --> 00:05:10.860
When all of their main adventures are over
and they all start families, I hope Bolin

00:05:10.860 --> 00:05:14.090
starts doing Movers full time.

00:05:14.090 --> 00:05:15.570
Number 5 - Meet Kai

00:05:15.570 --> 00:05:21.280
It's a little surreal thinking about people
as airbenders when they're dressed like Earth

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:22.280
Benders.

00:05:22.280 --> 00:05:26.220
Last Airbender treated colors and bending
styles a little more rigidly, but the whole

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:32.020
idea is that they're searching for airbenders
inside the Earth Kingdom.

00:05:32.020 --> 00:05:38.150
As of right now Kai is fun, but I don't think
he's going to be my favorite new character.

00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:42.100
He feels a little less compelling than the
evil benders.

00:05:42.100 --> 00:05:47.340
I know they're technically not evil, but just
to distinguish them for now I'm calling them

00:05:47.340 --> 00:05:48.340
that.

00:05:48.340 --> 00:05:53.820
Whenever we met Toph she lied about her past
to keep people from judging her.

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:57.540
I wonder if Kai will have something similar
going on, where his parents were killed as

00:05:57.540 --> 00:06:00.490
part of something related to the main story.

00:06:00.490 --> 00:06:08.560
It's totally possible that they won't pay
that off.

00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:11.910
But if he lied about the gold, he could have
lied about his parents being killed by raiders,

00:06:11.910 --> 00:06:15.270
so we need more information about him before
I pass judgement.

00:06:15.270 --> 00:06:19.100
As for the Jinora shipping that's going on,
I'm not as excited about it as Korasami but

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:20.220
I think it's fine.

00:06:20.220 --> 00:06:26.580
It's not something I'm going to be investing
a lot of gif making energy into.

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:28.770
Number 4 - The Republic City Spirit

00:06:28.770 --> 00:06:32.190
Right at the beginning when Korra is first
dealing with the vines the spirit, who was

00:06:32.190 --> 00:06:35.260
awesome, completely sets up the premise of
the season.

00:06:35.260 --> 00:06:39.580
Tenzin did it too, there will probably be
several characters like Zaheer who also call

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:42.460
out what the arc of Book 3 is.

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:46.120
"There is no difference between the Spirits
and the People, we're all the same.

00:06:46.120 --> 00:06:48.450
The Avatar of all people should know that."

00:06:48.450 --> 00:06:50.470
The idea is that Korra has to learn this and
it's going to take all season for the lesson

00:06:50.470 --> 00:06:58.680
to cook inside her brain until it turns into
something actionable.

00:06:58.680 --> 00:07:03.370
First she learns a new lesson, like achieving
true inner peace in Book 1, then she is able

00:07:03.370 --> 00:07:04.720
to do something with it.

00:07:04.720 --> 00:07:06.560
In that case it was airbending.

00:07:06.560 --> 00:07:12.930
In book 3 it could mean a number of things,
mostly getting people and spirits used to

00:07:12.930 --> 00:07:14.180
living with each other.

00:07:14.180 --> 00:07:19.400
Once she's able to do that I expect that visually
we'll see the vines stop destroying buildings

00:07:19.400 --> 00:07:20.400
in Republic City.

00:07:20.400 --> 00:07:24.050
Quick sidenote, we haven't seen a lot of them
yet, but there will be tons of really cool

00:07:24.050 --> 00:07:27.620
looking spirits floating around the world.

00:07:27.620 --> 00:07:32.710
Number 3 - The Twins Are Back

00:07:32.710 --> 00:07:36.960
It took a few episodes last year for me to
get used to them, it wasn't till after Eska

00:07:36.960 --> 00:07:40.370
flipped out and chased after Bolin and Korra
that I really started loving her.

00:07:40.370 --> 00:07:42.560
Aubrey Plaza is so appropriate for her.

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:46.530
I've seen some shows and movies where she
doesn't play that type of flat emotionless

00:07:46.530 --> 00:07:50.650
character, but most of all I just picture
April from Parks and Rec.

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:53.060
I love that they're ruling the Northern Water
Tribe.

00:07:53.060 --> 00:07:58.200
I think this is because the leadership there
is hereditary.

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:02.110
Did anyone else think they heard Desna called
Zuko, Uncle Zuko?

00:08:02.110 --> 00:08:05.940
The room I was watching the episode in was
really loud so I wasn't sure, but I love the

00:08:05.940 --> 00:08:07.280
idea that they would do that.

00:08:07.280 --> 00:08:12.450
I think it's true because Zuko said that he
built the special underground prison for Ming

00:08:12.450 --> 00:08:16.419
Jua with Unalaq, which means he would have
had to visit the Northern Water Tribe a long

00:08:16.419 --> 00:08:17.470
time ago.

00:08:17.470 --> 00:08:21.040
In the trailers there were shots of the twins
fighting with everyone when the evil benders

00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:27.040
break sparky sparky boom girl out, so maybe
we'll see an eventual reunion of Eska and

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:28.140
Bolin.

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:29.440
Number 2 - Zaheer escapes

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:36.119
I loved that this was right as Tenzin gave
that hopeful speech about finding new airbenders.

00:08:36.119 --> 00:08:41.209
They didn't say it right away, but Zaheer
is the leader of the evil bending team and

00:08:41.209 --> 00:08:44.080
he was not an airbender until Harmonic Convergence.

00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:50.329
His comment about Guru Maheema was a nice
callback to Guru Pathik, but he's mostly heralding

00:08:50.329 --> 00:08:55.790
the same thing Tenzin was talking about, change
is coming.

00:08:55.790 --> 00:08:58.089
Not everyone is going to like it.

00:08:58.089 --> 00:09:02.600
It's unclear why he wants to kill the Avatar
and the Order of the White Lotus.

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:07.449
It's not just another version of what UnaVaatu
was doing, helping the spirits dominate the

00:09:07.449 --> 00:09:08.449
physical realm.

00:09:08.449 --> 00:09:11.860
But I'm hoping that the next couple of episodes
spell out their thesis.

00:09:11.860 --> 00:09:19.439
I'm talking about episode 3 in a separate
video but during that episode, Korra realized

00:09:19.439 --> 00:09:21.290
she might be fighting for the wrong side.

00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:25.089
In that case it was the Earth Queen versus
the people, but I'm wondering if the evil

00:09:25.089 --> 00:09:29.160
benders will try to get Korra to believe she's
fighting for the wrong cause.

00:09:29.160 --> 00:09:33.600
I guess that would be another version of what
UnaVaatu was doing, get her to help the spirits

00:09:33.600 --> 00:09:35.029
at the expense of helping people.

00:09:35.029 --> 00:09:40.670
It's still a little too early to tell.

00:09:40.670 --> 00:09:44.800
Who else loved the magneto style prisons all
those benders were in.

00:09:44.800 --> 00:09:49.399
I'm assuming Zuko built all of them himself
with the help of people in each nation.

00:09:49.399 --> 00:09:53.119
and my Number 1 Moment - Lord Zuko Returns

00:09:53.119 --> 00:09:57.390
Why he waited till after Harmonic Convergence
to make an appearance I have no idea, we're

00:09:57.390 --> 00:09:59.459
just happy he finally came to the party.

00:09:59.459 --> 00:10:02.379
Of all the classic Avatar characters, he's
one of my favorite.

00:10:02.379 --> 00:10:06.559
And even though Dante Basco isn't voicing
him, I still think he's going to be awesome.

00:10:06.559 --> 00:10:12.779
I think he'll explain more of what his true
mission has been while Korra Books 1 and 2

00:10:12.779 --> 00:10:13.779
have been happening.

00:10:13.779 --> 00:10:15.990
And it may also explain a little where Toph
has been.

00:10:15.990 --> 00:10:20.769
I saw a little of young Zuko's temper when
he found out the Water Bender had been Freed.

00:10:20.769 --> 00:10:24.569
They were in the fire nation, so it makes
sense that was were he would first appear,

00:10:24.569 --> 00:10:31.529
even though at that point Zaheer had already
freed two of the people.

00:10:31.529 --> 00:10:37.810
I'm really to hear him fill in a lot of the
backstory on those four benders.

00:10:37.810 --> 00:10:42.869
But now it's your turn, let me know what your
favorite moment was from the first two episodes!

00:10:42.869 --> 00:10:48.029
I'll be talking about The Earth Queen and
the Dai Li in my video tomorrow, but overall

00:10:48.029 --> 00:10:49.230
these first two episodes were worth the wait.

00:10:49.230 --> 00:10:53.139
I gave them a solid A for answering some big
questions right away and pretty clearly laying

00:10:53.139 --> 00:10:58.230
out what the progression of the next several
episodes will be.

00:10:58.230 --> 00:11:02.319
Team Avatar will try to find and help all
the new airbenders, rebuild the air nation

00:11:02.319 --> 00:11:06.569
and contain Zaheer's team.

00:11:06.569 --> 00:11:13.319
I think that the big challenge will be juggling
all the new Lin Beifong stuff we have yet

00:11:13.319 --> 00:11:17.500
to see and tie everything together by the
end of the season.

00:11:17.500 --> 00:11:22.750
One of the big problems with having so many
plots is that they all have to connect by

00:11:22.750 --> 00:11:23.750
the end.

00:11:23.750 --> 00:11:27.720
All the little side stories have to inform
the main story.

00:11:27.720 --> 00:11:32.800
In book 2 I feel like there were a few things
that didn't get paid off, like Varrick.

00:11:32.800 --> 00:11:34.720
I feel like his story ultimately wasn't necessary.

00:11:34.720 --> 00:11:38.589
Like it was created just to give Mako, Bolin
and Asami something to do.

00:11:38.589 --> 00:11:43.560
He didn't really have an impact on Harmonic
Convergence or the fight against Unavaatu.

00:11:43.560 --> 00:11:49.420
The thing I'm really liking about Book 3 so
far is that all the major characters have

00:11:49.420 --> 00:11:52.790
been established and I can see a couple of
ways they'll all come together by the end

00:11:52.790 --> 00:11:53.790
of the season.

00:11:53.790 --> 00:12:02.620
Korra will have to educate the Earth Queen
on treating her people better, she'll help

00:12:02.620 --> 00:12:06.819
the people in republic city learn to live
with the spirits and she'll make peace with

00:12:06.819 --> 00:12:08.319
Zaheer's team.

00:12:08.319 --> 00:12:12.499
So like I said, Episode 3 review posting tomorrow.

00:12:12.499 --> 00:12:14.239
Be sure to subscribe to get it.

00:12:14.239 --> 00:12:21.160
For the giveaway, I'm picking two random subscribers
from the comments on this video to give giftcards

00:12:21.160 --> 00:12:22.160
to.

00:12:22.160 --> 00:12:26.540
And one person from the comments on tomorrow's
video.

00:12:26.540 --> 00:12:28.249
Right now click here to get that video.

00:12:28.249 --> 00:12:31.040
I'll add the annotation as soon as I post
it.

00:12:31.040 --> 00:12:33.629
And click here for my top 5 book 3 characters
so far.

00:12:33.629 --> 00:12:35.990
Thanks for watching, I'll see you guys tomorrow.

